WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:02.235 line:0%
-So, yesterday,

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.270 line:0%
we checked in on my old friend
the Sea Captain,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.371 line:0%
as he was making his way

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.106 line:0%
through my copy
of "The Thorn Birds,"

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.874 line:0%
back in the captain's quarters,

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.077
but I want to make clear
to everyone who is worried --

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.079
the Sea Captain
is not coming back.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.948
I haven't spoken to him since
I left those captain quarters,

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:17.384
although, when I went
down to the bank

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.286
of the East River this morning
for my daily constitutional,

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:23.455
I did find this message
in a bottle

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:24.557
floating in the water.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.093
And let's see here
what it says.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.762
"Hey, Seth, what did the pirate
say to his ex-wife

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.330
when they spotted a lighthouse?

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.432
'Land, ho!'"
Jesus, man.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.268
God help whoever he
ends up with next.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.036
And, hey, speakin'
of needing help --

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.337
studio segue --

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.473
the president held
an old-fashioned campaign rally

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.342
in North Carolina,
as if the coronavirus pandemic

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.743
that's still raging
out of control

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:46.145
had just magically disappeared.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.681
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:52.752 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.188
Now is typically the time
in the political calendar

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.422
when an incumbent president

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.191
who's trailing badly
in the polls

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.425
starts to get desperate

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.994
and Donald Trump couldn't
look any more desperate

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.963
if he was crammed
into a phone booth,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.832
beggin' for the Glengarry leads.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.500
No human being on Earth

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.668
reeks of desperation
more than Donald Trump.

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:12.671
He sweats like a guy at the OTB
who bet everything on a horse

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:14.673
named Ol' Three Legs.

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:16.175
Now, we all know
that Trump doesn't just lie.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:19.478
He belches out the most
outlandish lies he can think of,

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:20.946
especially when he's desperate.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.382
But on Tuesday,
at a rally in North Carolina,

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.451
he managed to outdo himself
when he told his supporters

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.987
that, despite
what they can see and hear

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.491
with their own eyes and ears,
Mexico really is paying

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.893
for the dumb border wall
he didn't build.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.095
And, honestly,
it was a real throwback,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.764
to hear the old
Mexico border wall lie again.

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:41.200
It was like hearin'
"Uptown Funk" on the radio

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.002
and thinkin', "Oh, man!

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.605
I used to hear
this song at the gym.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.540
And I used to go to the gym.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.143
And I used to leave
my apartment. [ Chuckle ]

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.379
Uptown funk you up, indeed."

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.481
But, yeah, "Mexico's paying
for the wall" is back.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.617
Now, to be clear, the parts
of the wall that have been built

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.119
or renovated were funded,
not by Mexico,

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.488
but by taxpayer dollars
that Congress allocated

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.689
for the Defense Department.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:06.726
Trump used a national
emergency declaration

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.095
to pull funds that were
supposed to be spent

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.730
on military
construction projects,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.665
schools and daycares,
among other things.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.933
That money -- your money --
went to his wall.

00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:17.136
But on Tuesday,
Trump tried to paper over that

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.805
with a new,
breathtakingly stupid lie

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:23.609
about how Mexico would
supposedly pay for the wall.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.878
-And, you know, Mexico
is paying for the wall,

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:27.246
just so you understand.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.281
They don't say that.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.682
They never say it.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.384
But we're gonna charge them
a small fee at the border,

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:33.385
you know, the tollbooths.

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:34.487
We have tollbooths.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.255
It's the biggest border
in the world,

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.957
in terms of people
going across it,

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.592
in terms of industry,
believe it or not,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.793
the southern border.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.428
We're putting a small toll on

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.231
and maybe we're going to do
something with remittance.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.698
That's where people come here,
make money,

00:02:46.698 --> 00:02:48.234
and they send it back.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.036
So we'll do something and we're
gonna get all the money

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:53.906
that we spent on the mall --
wall -- will be coming back.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:56.141
-Wait, so, now,
you're gonna put tollbooths

00:02:56.141 --> 00:02:58.377
on the southern border
and charge people a fee

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:00.146
when they drive across?

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.481
That's your plan?
It's one of the largest

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.781
international borders
in the world,

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:04.283
not the Verrazzano Bridge.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.519
They're comin' from Mexico,
not Staten Island.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.987
[ Laughing ]
Thank God.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.188
[ As Trump ]
We're gonna charge 'em a toll

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:10.523
and no E-ZPass, folks.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.824
We're gonna have those little,

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.526
little baskets
where you toss a coin.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.660
You remember those.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.329
And you have to have
the exact change.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.663
You absolutely have
to have the exact.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:19.899
And if you miss and you're
out of coins in your car,

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.367
you gotta get out of your car

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.036
and you gotta pick it up
while everyone honks at you.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.170
We're also gonna put in some

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.904
of those coin-operated
binoculars,

00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:27.239
so, if they miss home,

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.274
they have to pay fifty cents
to look back at Mexico.

00:03:29.274 --> 00:03:31.610
Maybe one of those
grocery store kiddie rides.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.579
Those guys are cash cows.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.814
It'll add up. It'll add up.
It'll buy a wall.

00:03:35.814 --> 00:03:37.016
Honestly, why does he
even come up

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.384
with these
elaborate explanations?

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.885
If you're gonna lie,
keep it simple.

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.820
Your hardcore fans
will believe anything.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.391
Just have Eric come onstage
in a sombrero and fake mustache,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.959
pretending to be
the president of Mexico,

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.594
presenting you
with a giant novelty check

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.562
for a gajillion pesos.

00:03:50.562 --> 00:03:53.099
[ As Trump ]
Oh, look, everyone,
the president of Mexico is here.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.967
"No, Dad.
It's me, Eric."

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.270
Oh! iIdioto!

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.939
So that's what the president was
talkin' about as the pandemic

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.074
[ Laughing ] continued
to rage outta control,

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.310
rising in at least 22 states.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.580
Now, we know these events
have seeded outbreaks.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.516
Trump's Tulsa rally in June
likely seeded an outbreak there,

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.418
according to the local
health director

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.986
and, yet, Trump keeps
doing them, anyway,

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.687
because he doesn't care
if people get sick.

00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:17.256
In fact, today we learned

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.158
that he admitted
to journalist Bob Woodward

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.961
that he downplayed
the threat from the virus.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.430
And, at the rally,
he actually expressed amazement

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.800
at how many people had come out
to his super spreader event.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.768
-I'm thrilled to be
in Winston-Salem

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:33.172
with thousands of loyal,
hardworking American patriots.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.406
[ Cheering and applause ]
You are great people.

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:35.475
Great people.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.310
[ Cheering and applause
continues ]

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.913
I don't know how many people
are here, but there's a lot.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.681
[ Cheering intensifies ]

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:45.718
There's a lot.
[ Whistling and applause ]

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.153
We said, "Let's keep it down."

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:50.356
They didn't do too good a job,
but that's good, right?

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.258
That's good.
No, these crowds, I tell ya.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.927
It's beyond what we had,
in terms of enthusiasm,

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:58.598
beyond what we had
four years ago in 2016,

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.599
and that was
a record enthusiasm.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:03.169
We are breaking that record
by a lot.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.038
[ As Trump ]
It's incredible how many people
are here, chanting and yelling

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:08.708
and coughing in close proximity
to each other.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.243
Also, we got a couple of beach
balls bouncin' around the crowd,

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:13.846
so make sure you get your hands
and your mouths on those.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.881
Now, as we head
down the home stretch

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.182
of the presidential campaign,
we're in a moment

00:05:17.182 --> 00:05:19.052
of acute national crisis,

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.720
unlike anything
we've seen in a century.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.456
There are multiple crises
colliding all at once --

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.624
a raging pandemic,
an economic crash,

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:26.793
the collapse of our democracy,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.260
the dismantling
of the post office,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.896
the breakdown of the
school system,

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:32.398
a housing crisis,
widespread food insecurity,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.967
extreme weather events
supercharged by climate change,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.569
a national reckoning
over systemic racism.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:40.439
There's even -- true story --
of national coin shortage.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.075
We just didn't notice
because everyone's

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:43.675
too scared to use coins now.

00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:46.045
And, when you do, you have
to wipe it down so much,

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.480
you can't even tell who's
on it anymore.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:50.015
I mean, I think that's maybe

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.951
the dude from ZZ Top?

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.219
Is that you, Billy Gibbons?!

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:55.021
-♪ Oh, hoh hoh hoh ♪

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.655
-Oh, [bleep]

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.491
Are the graphics gonna
start talkin' now.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:00.125
Hey, ZZ Top Lincoln,
what's the difference

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:02.161
between you in real life
and you on a penny?

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.664
-♪ Legs ♪

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.332
We have limited crew back,
but the people who say no

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.900
to jokes like that
are still out of the building.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.535
In fact, things are so bad,

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.370
even Trump seems aware,
on some level,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.372
that we've careened way
over the precipice

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:14.907
and plunged down into the abyss.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:17.977
In the middle of a rant
about God knows what --

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.713
honestly, I couldn't explain it
and it's not worth trying --

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.882
he was, I guess,
telling his crowd

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.650
to imagine
what it would be like

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.986
if they return to Earth
3,000 years from now.

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:29.755
-If you come back
in 1,000 years,

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:33.425
2,000 years, or 3,000 years,
if you're lucky enough --

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.127
[ Laughing ]
assuming we have something.

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:37.396
The world is a crazy place,
isn't it?

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:38.631
-What?!

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:42.234
Is it slam poetry night
in the head injury ward?

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:45.137
Yeah, man!
We know the world is crazy.

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:48.007
Did you just wake up
from a four-year KFC coma?

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.209
"Last thing I remember, I was
chugging gravy out of a bucket

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:52.744
and then, I fell asleep
on the Trump Tower escalator."

00:06:52.744 --> 00:06:54.046
The world is a crazy place

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.181
and you're a big reason
for that.

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:58.050
Trump makes everything crazy.
He's like the friend

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.718
who shows up at your place
at 3:00 am

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:02.555
with a vape pen, a handle
of vodka, and a duffel bag,

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.190
askin' if he can crash with you.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.857
And then, when you're gettin'
ready for work in the morning,

00:07:05.857 --> 00:07:08.494
he says, "Bro, you look tired."

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:11.230
But, in particular,
two of the simultaneous crises

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.200
we're currently dealing with
are a rapid slide into autocracy

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.467
and an out-of-control pandemic

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.336
and, in many ways,
they're related.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.538
Like any would-be dictator,
Trump doesn't care

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.540
about the public health
response to the pandemic

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.275
or preventing the deaths

00:07:23.275 --> 00:07:25.077
of hundreds
of thousands of Americans,

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.578
unless it benefits
him personally.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:29.915
That's why he hawked
one miracle cure after another,

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:33.018
touted by cable pundits
and a pillow salesman

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:35.253
and a doctor who believes
in demon sperm.

00:07:35.253 --> 00:07:37.757
It doesn't matter that they're
crazy or incompetent,

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:38.925
just that they praised him.

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:41.560
If Trump met a herbalist
who complimented his tie,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.362
he'd show up to his next
press conference

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.230
with some tinctures and sage.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.965
[ As Trump ]
Alright, everyone,
we're gonna smudge the room

00:07:46.965 --> 00:07:48.968
and then drink
some honeysuckle extract

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.302
while holding one
of these crystals.

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:51.904
They're just rocks I dug up
in the Rose Garden.

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.472
We're calling 'em
crystals, though.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.340
In fact, Trump is, once again,
desperately hoping

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.509
for a coronaviruses
silver bullet

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:59.177
to revive his
political fortunes.

00:07:59.177 --> 00:08:02.180
He's pressuring the CDC and FDA

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.851
to approve a coronavirus
vaccine before November,

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.454
despite the fact that experts
have said that's unlikely.

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:09.655
And, yet, on Monday,
Trump announced

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:12.691
that a vaccine could be
ready by October,

00:08:12.691 --> 00:08:15.127
which just happens to be right
before the election.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.362
-Under my leadership,
we'll produce a vaccine

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:18.697
in record time.

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:21.500
'Cause, now, they see
we've done an incredible job,

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.969
and in speed like nobody's
ever seen before.

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:26.271
This could've taken two
or three years

00:08:26.271 --> 00:08:28.874
and, instead, it's going
to be -- [ Laughs ]

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:31.943
it's gonna be done
in a very short period of time.

00:08:31.943 --> 00:08:35.414
Could even have it
during the month of October.

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.716
-Oh! October.
How convenient.

00:08:37.716 --> 00:08:40.753
He's like an inveterate gambler
who's in deep with a loan shark.

00:08:40.753 --> 00:08:42.455
"I quit gambling
and I can get you your money.

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:44.824
You just gotta give me until the
day after the Kentucky Derby.

00:08:44.824 --> 00:08:47.259
Don't let me down again,
Ol' Three Legs!"

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:49.362
And, look, we all desperately
want a vaccine

00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:51.330
as soon as humanly possible,
but we want it

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.000
to be safe and effective,
so enough people will get it

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.534
and we can put
this nightmare behind us.

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:57.402
Unfortunately,
the way Trump is going,

00:08:57.402 --> 00:08:59.571
he's gonna start handin' out
vials of Diet Coke

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:01.707
at his rallies,
labeled "vaxine."

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:04.377
Trump sees no distinction
between the government

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.811
and his personal interests.

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.446
America's slide into autocracy

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.482
and the administration's
horrific response

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:12.284
to the coronavirus pandemic
are related crises.

00:09:12.284 --> 00:09:13.585
Aspiring dictators like Trump

00:09:13.585 --> 00:09:15.254
only care about what serves
their interests.

00:09:15.254 --> 00:09:17.790
Trump and the GOP are
an authoritarian movement

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.158
and, in a functioning democracy,

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:21.226
the people responsible
for this crisis

00:09:21.226 --> 00:09:22.662
would be banished
